lisa-design:
- The SCHEMA_URL custom manager lives in a repo-level renovate.json, not renovate/default.json: the URL exists only in this repo, and the preset is global config for every repo. GlobalConfig sets requireConfig "optional" and refuses none of the keys the repo file uses (only runnerKeys), and the preset sets no customManagers, so the repo file merges on top with nothing to conflict. Confirmed with Renovate 44.145.1 (local platform, extract): "Found renovate.json config file", 3 regex package files.
- The custom manager uses the same depName/packageName (golangci/golangci-lint) and datasource (github-releases) as the github-actions manager's golangci-lint-action uses-with dep (known-actions/github-releases.ts: no depName, so depName = packageName; no versioning, so the datasource default, same as the regex manager's), so both deps join renovate/all-non-major at the same version. No versioningTemplate on purpose: it would diverge from the uses-with dep's.
- managerFilePatterns (not the removed fileMatch, absent from the 44.145.1 schema) is a /regex/ on .github/workflows/ci-go-*.y?(a)ml. TestSchemaURLRenovate requires every workflow with a golangci-lint raw schema URL to be matched, so a new file can't silently escape it.
- The YAML check is Go-side: yaml.v3 rejects every non-YAML-1.2 escape except \' (scannerc.go accepts it as an extension), so the test parses with yaml.v3 and scans only double-quoted scalars' source for \'. Block scalars (run: scripts) are not checked: a shell \' there is the script's. Positions match yaml@2's BAD_DQ_ESCAPE positions (checked on origin/main: cut-prerelease.yml:20:57 etc.).
- No node tooling added to the repo; the yaml@2 strict parse and Renovate runs were done from a scratch dir / the renovate 44.145.1 container.

